Senior DevOps Interview Questions

At 4–6 years, interviewers test depth, production exposure, troubleshooting & decision-making, not basic commands.

Explain Linux boot process in detail
Difference between BIOS and UEFI
What happens after kernel is loaded?
User space vs kernel space
What is systemd and why is it important?
Difference between process and thread
How do you troubleshoot high CPU usage?
How do you identify memory leaks in Linux?
Zombie vs orphan process
What happens when a process is killed?
Inode — what is it and why it matters?
Hard link vs soft link (real use cases)
Difference between ext4 and xfs
Disk is full but df -h shows free space — why?
How do you troubleshoot disk I/O issues?
How does DNS resolution work in Linux?
How do you debug network connectivity issues?
Difference between TCP and UDP at OS level
What is iptables / nftables used for?
How do you check open ports and connections?
Explain Linux permission model in depth
What is SUID, SGID, sticky bit?
How do you secure a Linux server?
SELinux — why do DevOps engineers fear it?
How do you audit user activity in Linux?
Server rebooted unexpectedly — what will you check?
Application running but service is not accessible
SSH login suddenly stopped working — why?
System is slow but CPU & memory look normal
Logs are not getting generated — troubleshooting steps

 Interview Tip (4–6 yrs):
If you explain WHY something happens internally, not just HOW to fix it, you clearly sound senior & production-ready.
